    {
      "id": "textbook-network-fundamentals",
      "category": "textbook_general_technical",
      "title": "网络基础教材节选",
      "pages": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "text": "A router forwards packets based on the destination IP address. The TCP handshake establishes a connection. This chapter provides an overview of the three-way handshake and concludes with a summary of packet loss factors."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "text": "Packet loss increases latency. The transmission control protocol (TCP) is contrasted with the user datagram protocol (UDP) in the next section. The chapter compares connection-oriented and connectionless transport."
        }
      ],
      "golden": {
